WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:49.671 --> 00:00:50.880
What is your --

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:52.132
Thank you.

00:00:52.132 --> 00:00:54.092
(Cheers and applause)

00:00:54.092 --> 00:00:56.303
What is your connection to dance?

00:00:56.886 --> 00:00:58.471
Do you love the ballet,

00:00:58.513 --> 00:01:01.516
or maybe you watch
those dance competitions on television?

00:01:01.975 --> 00:01:06.229
Or did you jump into the hora
at that bar mitzvah one time?

00:01:08.315 --> 00:01:11.359
I want you to reconsider
your connection to dance,

00:01:11.401 --> 00:01:13.945
because I believe it to be
a simple and successful way

00:01:13.987 --> 00:01:15.739
of accessing happiness within.

00:01:16.781 --> 00:01:19.034
What do you need to participate?

00:01:19.075 --> 00:01:20.869
Virtually nothing ...

00:01:20.869 --> 00:01:23.330
but your will to explore
and have a little fun.

00:01:23.788 --> 00:01:25.081
No music,

00:01:25.123 --> 00:01:27.208
no partner required.

00:01:29.127 --> 00:01:32.380
When I choreograph for film,
television and commercials,

00:01:32.422 --> 00:01:35.634
I often generate moves
that are based on the human experience.

00:01:36.051 --> 00:01:38.928
I take these moves,
I string them together,

00:01:38.928 --> 00:01:40.847
twist and play with their pace,

00:01:40.889 --> 00:01:43.099
in order to create more meaningful work.

00:01:43.850 --> 00:01:45.560
Let me show you what I mean.

00:01:45.602 --> 00:01:47.562
Here's a music video, "Chandelier,"

00:01:47.562 --> 00:01:49.230
that I choreographed for Sia,

00:01:49.272 --> 00:01:52.067
featuring the incredible dancer
Maddie Ziegler.

00:01:52.108 --> 00:01:53.234
("Chandelier" by Sia)

00:01:53.276 --> 00:01:56.571
(Lyrics) Won’t open my eyes
Keep my glass full until morning light

00:01:56.613 --> 00:01:59.366
Because I'm just holding on for tonight

00:01:59.407 --> 00:02:02.118
Help me, I'm holding on for dear life

00:02:02.118 --> 00:02:04.871
Won't look down, won't open my eyes

00:02:04.871 --> 00:02:07.457
Keep my glass full until morning light

00:02:07.457 --> 00:02:10.210
Because I'm just holding on for tonight

00:02:10.251 --> 00:02:11.795
On for tonight

00:02:11.836 --> 00:02:12.962
Sun is up

00:02:14.506 --> 00:02:17.634
Ryan Heffington: Now, let's play
that video one more time.

00:02:17.676 --> 00:02:19.969
And I want to show you
what inspired those moves.

00:02:20.011 --> 00:02:23.181
You may be surprised
at how rudimentary the sources are.

00:02:23.515 --> 00:02:25.266
(No music)

00:02:25.308 --> 00:02:27.977
RH: And fork, fork, fork,
stab it in the wall,

00:02:27.977 --> 00:02:29.688
toss it and pass out,

00:02:29.729 --> 00:02:30.897
come to

00:02:30.897 --> 00:02:32.065
and look;

00:02:32.065 --> 00:02:34.776
Charlie Chaplin, Charlie Chaplin,
cockroach up the wall,

00:02:34.776 --> 00:02:35.902
clean your mustache,

00:02:35.944 --> 00:02:37.362
a possum, sink ...

00:02:38.071 --> 00:02:39.864
Is it time for lunch yet?

00:02:39.906 --> 00:02:43.660
(Laughter)

00:02:43.702 --> 00:02:44.911
Thanks.

00:02:44.953 --> 00:02:46.871
(Applause)

00:02:46.871 --> 00:02:50.583
See, even a cute little cockroach
can inspire a dance move.

00:02:50.625 --> 00:02:52.585
But it really is that easy.

00:02:52.585 --> 00:02:53.753
And, look ...

00:02:54.295 --> 00:02:56.297
Most people can't dance like Maddie,

00:02:56.339 --> 00:02:57.674
including myself.

00:02:58.466 --> 00:03:00.176
And that's the point.

00:03:00.510 --> 00:03:04.013
We all have our own
beautiful ways of moving,

00:03:04.013 --> 00:03:06.558
and this is worth celebrating.

00:03:07.434 --> 00:03:11.813
It’s time to extract the judgment
out of our dance experience

00:03:11.813 --> 00:03:15.567
and set free the preconceived notion
of what "good" dance is.

00:03:15.984 --> 00:03:17.110
And instead ...

00:03:18.778 --> 00:03:22.240
find out how your own body loves to move,

00:03:22.282 --> 00:03:25.201
and find out that inner rhythm

00:03:25.201 --> 00:03:26.745
that feels so good.

00:03:27.579 --> 00:03:29.831
Think more body ...

00:03:30.665 --> 00:03:32.000
less critique.

00:03:34.419 --> 00:03:39.215
So you may ask, "Well, how do I access
or unlock this dance magic?"

00:03:39.716 --> 00:03:43.636
Well, once you have the perspective
that life is dance,

00:03:43.678 --> 00:03:44.846
yeah?

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:48.433
You'll begin to see dance
everywhere around you, all day long,

00:03:48.475 --> 00:03:49.601
like I do.

00:03:50.393 --> 00:03:51.895
Like now.

00:03:51.936 --> 00:03:54.105
Witness how you're sitting in front of me.

00:03:54.647 --> 00:03:55.774
Your posture.

00:03:56.483 --> 00:03:58.401
Are both feet grounded?

00:03:58.401 --> 00:04:00.695
Is one leg crossed over the other?

00:04:01.321 --> 00:04:02.906
Where are your hands placed?

00:04:04.407 --> 00:04:05.575
Or envision ...

00:04:06.701 --> 00:04:08.661
a parent rocking their child.

00:04:10.747 --> 00:04:12.832
It's a playful flourish, right?

00:04:13.249 --> 00:04:14.501
Tying your shoe.

00:04:16.252 --> 00:04:17.545
A grand gesture.

00:04:18.421 --> 00:04:20.131
Drinking a glass of water.

00:04:22.967 --> 00:04:24.886
The stylized head release.

00:04:28.431 --> 00:04:30.767
So check out this proof of concept.

00:04:31.893 --> 00:04:35.396
In the first week of the worldwide
lockdown in March 2020,

00:04:35.438 --> 00:04:39.818
I decided to teach this online
follow-along dance class called SWEATFEST.

00:04:40.527 --> 00:04:41.694
I was hoping --

00:04:41.694 --> 00:04:45.406
(Cheers and applause)

00:04:45.448 --> 00:04:48.159
I was hoping that a couple
of friends would join in,

00:04:48.201 --> 00:04:50.495
but over the course
of the next couple of weeks,

00:04:50.495 --> 00:04:54.165
tens of thousands of people
from all over the world

00:04:54.207 --> 00:04:55.375
joined SWEATFEST ...

00:04:56.167 --> 00:04:58.378
turning our collective isolation

00:04:58.378 --> 00:05:00.213
into a worldwide community.

00:05:01.506 --> 00:05:03.383
It was absolutely beautiful.

00:05:04.425 --> 00:05:06.177
People checked their critical minds

00:05:06.219 --> 00:05:09.097
and really unleashed that joy from within,

00:05:09.138 --> 00:05:11.933
doing these goofy dance moves,

00:05:11.975 --> 00:05:14.143
while the world was in disarray.

00:05:14.185 --> 00:05:15.353
Take a look.

00:05:15.353 --> 00:05:16.521
(Music)

00:05:28.032 --> 00:05:29.284
(Music ends)

00:05:29.325 --> 00:05:30.368
(Laughs)

00:05:30.368 --> 00:05:33.079
Who would have guessed
that moves like the Pretty Pony

00:05:33.079 --> 00:05:34.372
and the Bob Ross ...

00:05:34.414 --> 00:05:35.790
would be so life-changing.

00:05:35.832 --> 00:05:39.335
(Laughter)

00:05:39.377 --> 00:05:42.463
So, I've been a student
of dance for 42 years.

00:05:42.505 --> 00:05:46.092
My relationship with the art form
runs deep and quite intimate.

00:05:46.676 --> 00:05:48.469
This helped me through trauma,

00:05:48.511 --> 00:05:49.888
it has paid my rent,

00:05:49.929 --> 00:05:53.516
but most of all, it's been
an unfaltering joy in my life.

00:05:54.392 --> 00:05:55.810
And that's why I'm here.

00:05:55.852 --> 00:05:58.229
Because I believe
there's more joy for you,

00:05:58.229 --> 00:05:59.731
only steps away,

00:06:00.773 --> 00:06:03.109
via simple and rudimentary moves

00:06:04.027 --> 00:06:05.486
that you already know.

00:06:06.487 --> 00:06:09.991
So, I'd love to invite you
to be your own choreographer.

00:06:10.658 --> 00:06:12.327
Grab your kids or go solo,

00:06:12.368 --> 00:06:16.331
and let fun and laughter push
the boundaries of ridiculousness.

00:06:16.873 --> 00:06:17.999
Who knows?

00:06:18.041 --> 00:06:19.292
Maybe brushing your teeth

00:06:19.334 --> 00:06:21.044
or whisking up mac and cheese

00:06:21.085 --> 00:06:23.212
will become your new favorite dance move.

00:06:24.130 --> 00:06:28.468
And once you have a dance move
or two or three or four under your belt,

00:06:28.509 --> 00:06:30.637
respectfully call yourself a dancer ...

00:06:31.429 --> 00:06:33.097
because you've earned it --

00:06:33.473 --> 00:06:38.061
and share those moves and that happiness
with those around you,

00:06:38.811 --> 00:06:40.855
because a world of more dance

00:06:40.855 --> 00:06:42.565
is a world of more joy.

00:06:42.607 --> 00:06:43.733
(Music)

00:06:44.609 --> 00:06:45.777
(Music stops)

00:06:46.152 --> 00:06:47.320
(Music)

00:08:06.899 --> 00:08:09.402
(Lyrics) Sit down and begin playing.

00:08:10.069 --> 00:08:13.197
If you feel good
about yourself and the world,

00:08:13.197 --> 00:08:14.657
it will show in your painting,

00:08:14.699 --> 00:08:17.952
and all these little things will happen.

00:08:17.994 --> 00:08:19.328
(Music continues)

00:08:38.681 --> 00:08:39.849
(Music ends)

00:08:39.849 --> 00:08:41.559
(Cheers and applause)

00:08:48.775 --> 00:08:49.942
RH: Thank you.

00:08:49.984 --> 00:08:56.115
(Cheers and applause continue)

